---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import Split from '../components/Split.astro'
import MomentsSection from '../components/MomentsSection.astro'
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro'
import { imageByFilename } from '../data/homePageImages'

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL

const familiesMomentsItems = [
  {
    image: imageByFilename('474778198_18155740735338056_3713170999697187589_n.jpg'),
    fallbackAlt: 'A parent holding a smiling baby during a Sunday gathering',
  },
  {
    image: imageByFilename('656838890_18200890015338056_1357170169128708571_n.jpg'),
    fallbackAlt: 'A volunteer playing with toddlers during a weekday playgroup',
  },
  {
    image: imageByFilename('689126575_18204342181338056_3955013236978091516_n.jpg'),
    fallbackAlt: 'Two young friends coloring together during a service',
  },
]
---

<BaseLayout title="Families | Pine Lake Covenant Church">
  <div class="canvas">
    <Split
      class="to-full"
      filename="718687687_18207937183338056_4793907761382693236_n.jpg"
      alt="Moms talking together, one holding a baby, near the Families banner"
      tone="sand"
      reverse
      eyebrow="Families"
    >
      <h1 class="display">Families</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Family life can be busy, beautiful, and sometimes <i>exhausting</i>. At Pine Lake, we want to be a place where
        families feel supported, welcomed, and free to take part at whatever pace makes sense for them.
      </p>
    </Split>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Find the right fit</p>
      <h2>Kids and youth at Pine Lake</h2>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <Photo
            filename="Pine-Lake-Kids-web.webp"
            alt="Pine Lake Kids"
            class="families__program-logo"
            widths={[240, 480, 720]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 80vw, 240px"
          />
          <p>
            Sunday morning programs for <strong>babies through 5th grade</strong>, plus midweek connection points and
            summer highlights.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href={`${base}families/kids/`}>Explore Pine Lake Kids →</a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <Photo
            filename="PineLakeYouth_logo_web.png"
            alt="Pine Lake Youth"
            class="families__program-logo"
            widths={[240, 480, 720]}
            sizes="(max-width: 768px) 80vw, 240px"
          />
          <p>
            For <strong>6th–12th grade</strong>. Tuesdays 6:00–8:00pm, plus students sit together on Sundays at 10:00am.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href={`${base}youth/`}>Explore Pine Lake Youth →</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Split
      class="to-full"
      id="kids"
      filename="717076557_18207937231338056_670985796948202660_n.jpg"
      alt="A volunteer reading a story to children during Pine Lake Kids"
      tone="paper"
      eyebrow="Sundays"
      heading="Families on Sunday mornings"
    >
      <p>
        On Sundays, we offer programming for children and youth of all ages, from babies through high school. Parents
        are always welcome to keep their children with them, or to use the programs that best fit their family.
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li>Programs available for <strong>ages 0–18</strong></li>
        <li><strong>Quick check-in</strong> in the foyer</li>
        <li>Consistent, caring volunteers who love kids</li>
        <li>
          A comfortable space where parents can <strong>watch the service while caring for babies and toddlers</strong>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>One Sunday each month, our elementary-aged kids stay in the service to worship alongside their families.</p>

      <p>
        We don’t see kids and youth as something separate happening down the hall. They’re an important part of the life
        of the church, and we love finding ways for families to worship and grow together.
      </p>
    </Split>

    <section class="section section-callout">
      <h2>Safety and care</h2>

      <p>We take the responsibility of caring for children seriously.</p>

      <ul>
        <li>All volunteers are <strong>background checked</strong></li>
        <li>A <strong>secure check-in and pickup system</strong> is used</li>
        <li>There are always <strong>at least two adults</strong> in each room</li>
      </ul>

      <p>Our goal is to create an environment where kids feel safe and known, and parents can relax and be present.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="eyebrow">Beyond Sunday mornings</p>
      <h2>Simple ways to connect</h2>

      <p class="measure">
        Sundays are just one part of family life at Pine Lake. Beyond weekly services, there are simple, low-pressure
        ways for families to connect, build friendships, and support one another through everyday life. Here are a few:
      </p>

      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Community Playgroup</h3>
          <p>
            A relaxed weekday gathering for parents and young children — a simple place to meet other families, let
            little ones play, and enjoy conversation (and coffee).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>MomCo</h3>
          <p>
            A community of moms supporting one another so no one has to do the journey of parenting alone. Practical
            encouragement, real friendships, and space to breathe.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Club 45</h3>
          <p>
            For 4th and 5th graders: a fun, welcoming gathering with games, friendships, and activities that help kids
            grow in confidence and faith.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Sports Camp</h3>
          <p>
            A summer highlight: a week of fun, movement, music, and age-appropriate Bible teaching — a great way for
            kids to build friendships and make memories.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="measure">
        Not sure where your family fits? Email <a href="mailto:office@plcc.org">office@plcc.org</a> and we’ll help you find
        a good first step — or just show up on a Sunday and we’ll point you in the right direction.
      </p>
    </section>

    <MomentsSection items={familiesMomentsItems} eyebrow="Life together" sectionClass="to-wide" />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* On a <Photo>-rendered <img>, so must be global. */
  :global(.families__program-logo) {
    display: block;
    width: clamp(11.25rem, 37.5vw, 15rem);
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
</style>
